2026-10-20T20:38:24.0035558Z             "body": "The rc.16 publisher prepared its evidence at main5cd671e, then the source-custody guard correctly refused generated output inside the checkout. No tag or release was created.\n\nThis change gives qualifier, native evidence, publisher, guide generation and artifact upload one explicitly supplied, owned private directory outside source. The workflow allocates it with mktemp and mode0700. The whole-tree source guard, semantic verification, original checks, publication order and immutable release contracts remain intact. Both affected harnesses are aligned, and directory-metadata coverage is added.\n\nCurrent source:d8544f8173b3c01faa88d50e7145ec455bc5e170; tree14140fc8a3ce95e0ca5b15a421dc97ed190ec735. The superseded4be317e scanner/harness failures remain retained. All three scanner review slots are NULL pending genuine fresh reports and independent current-source review.\n\nValidation: original hosted required suite39482440273/job118834171449 passed163/163 with zero failures/skips; configured exact-source review6298783337 completed clear. Local targeted benign metadata/guide/orchestration tests passed7/7; five CJS syntax checks and YAML parse passed, preserving validation10min/publication95min. Fresh actual Python push scanner/collector39482430425:1 passed, with its complete packet retained at94a976797798e409dc141053a158b17b4b7a3205. JavaScript and remaining original checks are still running/queued. No merge or publication before all required gates pass.",
